1
00:00:16,474 --> 00:00:20,645
BLUE BOX SEASON 2

2
00:01:43,019 --> 00:01:44,020
{\an8}DECEMBER 31

3
00:01:44,103 --> 00:01:47,607
EPISODE 32
I NEED TO TELL YOU SOMETHING

4
00:01:48,274 --> 00:01:50,193
Well, then.

5
00:01:51,486 --> 00:01:53,446
Who's holding up the game?

6
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:54,697
Grandpa, obviously.

7
00:01:55,824 --> 00:01:57,659
<i>It's that time of year again.</i>

8
00:01:57,742 --> 00:02:00,703
<i>We play cards while the TV
plays in the background.</i>

9
00:02:01,412 --> 00:02:04,707
<i>No different
from every other New Year's Eve.</i>

10
00:02:05,416 --> 00:02:07,669
<i>I'm starting to wonder
if I just dreamed up</i>

11
00:02:07,752 --> 00:02:11,339
<i>what happened on Christmas Eve,
or even this whole living situation.</i>

12
00:02:13,424 --> 00:02:14,843
<i>But it's not a dream.</i>

13
00:02:15,718 --> 00:02:17,178
Did it offend you?

14
00:02:19,055 --> 00:02:21,349
<i>I haven't had a chance
to talk to her since then.</i>

15
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:24,978
Pass.

16
00:02:25,061 --> 00:02:27,355
Yes, I'm out!

17
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:32,861
<i>I'll text her "Happy New Year."</i>

18
00:02:33,444 --> 00:02:35,446
It's almost time.

19
00:02:36,447 --> 00:02:38,366
<i>Six, five...</i>

20
00:02:38,449 --> 00:02:39,576
<i>And then...</i>

21
00:02:39,659 --> 00:02:42,453
<i>Three, two, one.</i>

22
00:02:42,537 --> 00:02:44,581
<i>Happy New Year!</i>

23
00:02:44,664 --> 00:02:45,623
What?

24
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:48,501
MOM
CHINATSU! HAPPY NEW YEAR!

25
00:02:49,085 --> 00:02:51,546
Chinatsu must be in Nagano right now.

26
00:02:51,629 --> 00:02:53,715
I hope her family's
having a good time together.

27
00:02:53,798 --> 00:02:56,259
<i>Why did Mom ruin it
by messaging her first?</i>

28
00:02:56,843 --> 00:02:58,261
DAD
HOW'S YOUR GRANDPA'S PLACE?

29
00:03:00,263 --> 00:03:01,764
<i>Everyone texting in the group chat</i>

30
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:04,934
<i>makes it awkward for me
to send a message to her directly.</i>

31
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:07,395
CHINATSU KANO
HAPPY NEW YEAR!

32
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:10,773
IT'S SNOWING HERE
SHOVELING IT HAS BEEN GOOD EXERCISE...

33
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:13,276
<i>Even when she's so far away,</i>

34
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:16,404
<i>I'm able to feel this happy.</i>

35
00:03:18,364 --> 00:03:20,909
NISHIDA SENPAI
LET'S GO TO THE SHRINE!!!

36
00:03:20,992 --> 00:03:23,411
TACHIBANA SHRINE ENTRANCE

37
00:03:26,915 --> 00:03:28,917
There you are!

38
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,419
About time you showed up, Taiki!

39
00:03:32,462 --> 00:03:34,422
I couldn't find my scarf.

40
00:03:34,505 --> 00:03:36,716
It's good to see you again, Karen.

41
00:03:36,799 --> 00:03:38,301
You seem taller.

42
00:03:38,384 --> 00:03:40,303
- What?
- Does he?

43
00:03:40,386 --> 00:03:42,764
You see him every day.

44
00:03:44,641 --> 00:03:47,310
Look at you, all grown up.

45
00:03:48,019 --> 00:03:49,395
Thank you.

46
00:03:52,106 --> 00:03:54,901
Come on, let's go already!

47
00:04:00,865 --> 00:04:03,076
Hold on. I want to buy a drink.

48
00:04:06,579 --> 00:04:07,789
I'll treat you.

49
00:04:08,581 --> 00:04:09,457
Why?

50
00:04:10,416 --> 00:04:14,462
Because my siblings really loved
the cookies you made us for Christmas.

51
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:24,222
{\an8}<i>OSHIRUKO</i> DRINK

52
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:33,564
There are a lot of people here.

53
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:35,733
It's going to take forever.

54
00:04:45,076 --> 00:04:49,998
<i>I pray for good health, badminton,
romance, my grades, and world peace.</i>

55
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:52,000
<i>Please,</i>

56
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:56,337
<i>may this be a year
I can push straight toward my goals.</i>

57
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:02,176
It's fortune-drawing time!

58
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:04,387
{\an8}MISFORTUNE

59
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:06,139
{\an8}Misfortune?

60
00:05:06,222 --> 00:05:08,850
I'm going to keep pulling
until I get Great Fortune!

61
00:05:08,933 --> 00:05:10,101
Can you do that?

62
00:05:10,184 --> 00:05:12,061
There are no rules against it.

63
00:05:13,604 --> 00:05:16,024
{\an8}GREAT MISFORTUNE

64
00:05:16,607 --> 00:05:19,027
{\an8}<i>Great Misfortune?</i>

65
00:05:19,110 --> 00:05:22,113
I'm going to pull a Great Fortune next!

66
00:05:22,613 --> 00:05:24,532
<i>The second time, I got Good Fortune.</i>

67
00:05:24,615 --> 00:05:27,535
<i>The third time, Uncertain Fortune.</i>

68
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:29,037
<i>Fourth time!</i>

69
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:31,039
{\an8}GREAT FORTUNE

70
00:05:31,789 --> 00:05:33,041
<i>I got Great Fortune!</i>

71
00:05:39,547 --> 00:05:42,550
<i>"Romance... Don't hesitate."</i>

72
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:46,888
TACHIBANA SHRINE

73
00:05:46,971 --> 00:05:49,932
What did you get, Hinacchi?

74
00:05:50,892 --> 00:05:52,143
{\an8}Ta-da!

75
00:05:52,226 --> 00:05:53,644
{\an8}GREAT FORTUNE

76
00:05:53,728 --> 00:05:54,562
{\an8}What about you?

77
00:05:55,188 --> 00:05:58,066
I only care
about what my fortune says about romance.

78
00:05:58,649 --> 00:06:01,569
"Romance... Your path is full of thorns."

79
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:06,574
I'm getting a new one!

80
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:09,577
<i>Great Fortune!</i>

81
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:11,996
EVERYONE'S HAPPY

82
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:13,581
Without further ado!

83
00:06:14,165 --> 00:06:17,668
It's street food time!

84
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:20,004
Let's drink <i>amazake!</i>

85
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:22,090
Don't get lost.

86
00:06:30,181 --> 00:06:31,599
What's the matter?

87
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:34,811
It seems like you're dragging your feet.

88
00:06:34,894 --> 00:06:37,855
Someone actually stepped on my ankle.

89
00:06:38,481 --> 00:06:40,483
I think it's scraped.

90
00:06:40,566 --> 00:06:43,778
I've got an adhesive bandage.
We can go over there to put it on.

91
00:06:43,861 --> 00:06:45,613
But everyone's...

92
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:49,992
Sorry, Moriya.

93
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:53,496
Tell everyone
we'll catch up to them later.

94
00:06:54,539 --> 00:06:56,582
Okay, got it.

95
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:06,008
<i>I got separated.</i>

96
00:07:06,092 --> 00:07:11,013
None of the upperclassmen
ever check to make sure we're keeping up.

97
00:07:12,431 --> 00:07:13,975
<i>I guess I'll text them.</i>

98
00:07:15,726 --> 00:07:17,645
{\an8}INOMATA FAMILY
SOMEONE SENT A STICKER

99
00:07:20,731 --> 00:07:21,732
{\an8}KAREN MORIYA
INCOMING CALL

100
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:22,650
{\an8}<i>Hey!</i>

101
00:07:23,484 --> 00:07:25,403
{\an8}Happy New Year, Chii!

102
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:29,323
{\an8}<i>Don't just video call me out of the blue.</i>

103
00:07:30,116 --> 00:07:33,953
I thought it was important to wish you
a happy New Year face-to-face.

104
00:07:34,745 --> 00:07:37,165
We all came to the shrine together.

105
00:07:37,999 --> 00:07:38,958
See?

106
00:07:44,338 --> 00:07:45,256
What?

107
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:47,216
We lost Taiki ages ago.

108
00:07:47,925 --> 00:07:50,470
<i>And here I was hoping
they could see each other.</i>

109
00:07:53,389 --> 00:07:55,224
{\an8}Did you draw some fortunes?

110
00:07:55,308 --> 00:07:56,809
<i>Funny you should ask!</i>

111
00:07:56,893 --> 00:07:57,852
TAIKI
NEW MESSAGE

112
00:07:58,895 --> 00:08:00,730
Did you just get a message?

113
00:08:00,813 --> 00:08:02,815
I can call you back later if you're busy.

114
00:08:09,947 --> 00:08:12,700
{\an8}TAIKI INOMATA
CAN WE TALK WHEN YOU GET BACK?

115
00:08:12,783 --> 00:08:15,745
{\an8}I NEED TO TELL YOU SOMETHING

116
00:08:16,579 --> 00:08:18,873
{\an8}READ 1:42 A.M.

117
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,199
{\an8}CHINATSU KANO
SURE

118
00:09:17,181 --> 00:09:19,058
There you are.

119
00:09:20,017 --> 00:09:22,895
First you're late, then you get lost.
You've got some nerve.

120
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:24,063
Sorry.

121
00:09:24,730 --> 00:09:27,191
Don't be late for the ski trip
on the 4th and 5th.

122
00:09:27,275 --> 00:09:29,569
I'll make sure to set 20 alarms.

123
00:09:30,444 --> 00:09:32,613
Where are Kyo and Hina?

124
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:37,326
Did you get separated too?

125
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:39,745
Nope, we just did our own thing.

126
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:42,373
This is the problem
with athletes who do individual sports.

127
00:09:42,456 --> 00:09:43,583
That's so true.

128
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:46,168
"Birds of a feather flock together."

129
00:09:46,252 --> 00:09:47,795
Wait, you're including me in that?

130
00:09:50,798 --> 00:09:51,716
EXIT

131
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:54,302
- Bye!
- See you at practice!

132
00:10:00,391 --> 00:10:04,145
Must be tough
managing such free-spirited people.

133
00:10:04,228 --> 00:10:05,605
Impressive, right?

134
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:08,399
You are surprisingly nurturing after all.

135
00:10:08,482 --> 00:10:10,276
What do you mean, "surprisingly"?

136
00:10:10,359 --> 00:10:13,321
Be careful, people like you
tend to fall for losers.

137
00:10:13,404 --> 00:10:16,115
I know that already.

138
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:20,119
Although, that boy with glasses
seemed okay.

139
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:22,246
You mean Kasahara?

140
00:10:22,830 --> 00:10:24,457
You have a crush on him, don't you?

141
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:27,126
You looked super jealous
seeing him with Hina.

142
00:10:27,710 --> 00:10:29,378
No way!

143
00:10:29,462 --> 00:10:33,966
<i>I'm more into hot boys
who are totally hot hotties.</i>

144
00:10:34,050 --> 00:10:35,134
MY NO. 1 LOVE
YUSA

145
00:10:38,304 --> 00:10:40,556
<i>The reason I made that face</i>

146
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:43,142
<i>is because I know how Hinacchi feels.</i>

147
00:10:43,851 --> 00:10:46,145
<i>Kasahara probably...</i>

148
00:10:48,314 --> 00:10:50,524
Absolutely no way.

149
00:10:51,192 --> 00:10:52,026
Yeah?

150
00:10:53,235 --> 00:10:55,112
If you say so.

151
00:11:00,117 --> 00:11:04,038
{\an8}JANUARY 1

152
00:11:04,121 --> 00:11:07,041
HAPPY NEW YEAR

153
00:11:07,124 --> 00:11:07,958
That looks good.

154
00:11:08,042 --> 00:11:10,044
- I did a good job, right?
- Yeah.

155
00:11:10,961 --> 00:11:12,129
Welcome.

156
00:11:12,630 --> 00:11:14,090
- Here!
- They fixed up that road.

157
00:11:14,173 --> 00:11:15,549
- Right?
- Thanks.

158
00:11:16,258 --> 00:11:17,218
{\an8}JANUARY 2

159
00:11:17,301 --> 00:11:18,552
{\an8}Let's go to the river!

160
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:19,512
{\an8}- Sure!
- Hold on!

161
00:11:19,595 --> 00:11:21,055
{\an8}Let's go to the park over there.

162
00:11:25,142 --> 00:11:28,062
{\an8}4TH: JYO-OU UNIVERSITY YOSHIKUNI HAYAMA
HIROSHIMA AKISEIRYU HIGH

163
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:37,571
<i>Time is going by so slowly.</i>

164
00:11:42,159 --> 00:11:45,496
<i>Chinatsu Senpai
doesn't get back until the 6th.</i>

165
00:11:45,579 --> 00:11:48,666
<i>Sure, I'm spending the 4th and 5th
skiing with the badminton team,</i>

166
00:11:48,749 --> 00:11:50,084
<i>but it's still four days away.</i>

167
00:11:52,628 --> 00:11:54,088
<i>I miss her so much.</i>

168
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:55,798
{\an8}CAN WE TALK WHEN YOU GET BACK?

169
00:11:55,881 --> 00:11:57,091
{\an8}I NEED TO TELL YOU SOMETHING

170
00:11:59,677 --> 00:12:02,096
<i>Maybe I don't want to see her.</i>

171
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:05,099
<i>Because the next time I do...</i>

172
00:12:11,105 --> 00:12:12,690
I'm going for a run.

173
00:12:15,151 --> 00:12:18,112
He could take a few days off
for the holidays at least.

174
00:12:18,195 --> 00:12:20,114
That's just how he is.

175
00:13:10,331 --> 00:13:12,124
<i>Until a year ago,</i>

176
00:13:12,750 --> 00:13:15,252
<i>we'd barely even spoken.</i>

177
00:13:17,963 --> 00:13:19,757
<i>And yet, before I knew it...</i>

178
00:13:40,903 --> 00:13:44,031
{\an8}EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

179
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:19,650
<i>Morning, Taiki!</i>

180
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:40,296
I'm home.

181
00:14:42,256 --> 00:14:46,468
I left the holiday cards we got
on the table.

182
00:14:50,264 --> 00:14:51,682
TO TAIKI INOMATA

183
00:14:57,771 --> 00:15:00,190
UNZEN, NAGANO
CHINATSU KANO

184
00:15:04,778 --> 00:15:07,323
{\an8}<i>"Happy New Year!"</i>

185
00:15:07,406 --> 00:15:10,576
{\an8}<i>"I couldn't have had
the school year I've had</i>

186
00:15:10,659 --> 00:15:13,203
{\an8}<i>if it weren't for all of you
in the Inomata family."</i>

187
00:15:22,504 --> 00:15:24,298
<i>I miss her so bad.</i>

188
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:28,719
{\an8}<i>Just these words make me want to see her.</i>

189
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:33,724
<i>Even when she's not around,
she's all I think about.</i>

190
00:15:34,808 --> 00:15:37,728
<i>Just her presence makes me happy.</i>

191
00:15:39,813 --> 00:15:41,148
<i>That's the kind of love</i>

192
00:15:41,732 --> 00:15:43,776
<i>I'm in right now.</i>

193
00:15:44,276 --> 00:15:46,737
{\an8}JANUARY 1, NAGANO

194
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:17,977
{\an8}TAIKI
CAN WE TALK WHEN YOU GET BACK?

195
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:19,269
{\an8}I NEED TO TELL YOU SOMETHING

196
00:16:34,243 --> 00:16:36,286
When are you getting out of bed?

197
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:38,998
I'm getting up now!

198
00:16:41,458 --> 00:16:42,710
Good morning.

199
00:16:42,793 --> 00:16:44,545
Good morning, Chii.

200
00:16:45,129 --> 00:16:46,880
What kind of mochi do you want?

201
00:16:46,964 --> 00:16:48,841
Sweet bean? Soy sauce?

202
00:16:48,924 --> 00:16:51,552
Let the poor girl sit down first.

203
00:16:56,473 --> 00:16:57,558
Thank you for this meal.

204
00:17:02,855 --> 00:17:06,316
You know, I grew
all these vegetables myself.

205
00:17:10,904 --> 00:17:13,574
You have quite the appetite.

206
00:17:14,366 --> 00:17:15,951
Because it's so good.

207
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:18,078
By the way, where's Dad?

208
00:17:18,662 --> 00:17:20,497
He went to say hi around the neighborhood.

209
00:17:20,998 --> 00:17:23,083
He hasn't been back here in a while.

210
00:17:23,876 --> 00:17:26,920
Now, tell us
about what's been going on with you.

211
00:17:27,004 --> 00:17:28,839
How's the basketball team going?

212
00:17:28,922 --> 00:17:30,090
What about your grades?

213
00:17:31,341 --> 00:17:33,093
I'm on top of it.

214
00:17:33,677 --> 00:17:35,262
Have you found anybody special?

215
00:17:36,013 --> 00:17:40,934
Honey, kids these days don't like
being asked questions like that.

216
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:43,228
- But aren't you worried?
- Oh, dear.

217
00:17:47,316 --> 00:17:48,776
You two met

218
00:17:48,859 --> 00:17:51,737
at Grandma's workplace, right?

219
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:53,947
<i>Right, at a traditional inn.</i>

220
00:17:54,031 --> 00:17:58,494
<i>Your grandpa came
and delivered vegetables every morning.</i>

221
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:01,580
When did you fall for Grandma?

222
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:06,835
Grandpas these days don't like
being asked questions like that.

223
00:18:06,919 --> 00:18:09,379
My, how convenient!

224
00:18:10,005 --> 00:18:12,758
I forget. It was a long time ago.

225
00:18:12,841 --> 00:18:15,969
Grandpa's shy
when it comes to these things.

226
00:18:18,764 --> 00:18:19,932
Chinatsu.

227
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:22,351
Once you're done,
can you go shovel the snow?

228
00:18:22,434 --> 00:18:23,894
Okay.

229
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:29,399
{\an8}JANUARY 2

230
00:18:51,004 --> 00:18:52,923
I'm going to go for a walk.

231
00:18:53,507 --> 00:18:55,092
It's so cold out.

232
00:18:55,175 --> 00:18:58,929
She doesn't like staying cooped up.

233
00:19:12,526 --> 00:19:14,361
Man, it's cold.

234
00:19:14,444 --> 00:19:16,822
We should've dressed more warmly.

235
00:19:16,905 --> 00:19:18,198
That's true.

236
00:19:19,449 --> 00:19:21,285
Are you okay?

237
00:19:21,368 --> 00:19:22,619
I'm not turning back now.

238
00:19:22,703 --> 00:19:23,954
Don't get sick.

239
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:45,142
Wow, look at the snow!

240
00:19:47,311 --> 00:19:49,104
Let's have a snowball fight!

241
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:53,066
- Give me a ten-second head start!
- What?

242
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:22,179
Use this if you like!

243
00:20:26,516 --> 00:20:28,268
Make sure you keep warm.

244
00:20:28,852 --> 00:20:30,479
<i>Taiki Inomata.</i>

245
00:20:41,907 --> 00:20:44,868
I can't believe you get up so early
every morning.

246
00:21:06,890 --> 00:21:08,308
Good morning.

247
00:21:16,858 --> 00:21:18,819
<i>He's here again today.</i>

248
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:21,446
<i>Taiki's here today too.</i>

249
00:21:23,073 --> 00:21:24,241
<i>And today too.</i>

250
00:21:37,170 --> 00:21:39,006
Chii!

251
00:21:39,089 --> 00:21:40,549
About what you asked earlier...

252
00:21:41,216 --> 00:21:43,510
There's more to it.

253
00:21:43,593 --> 00:21:45,053
What I asked earlier?

254
00:21:45,637 --> 00:21:49,224
What your grandpa said
when he told me how he felt.

255
00:21:51,518 --> 00:21:56,189
{\an8}JANUARY 3

256
00:22:05,657 --> 00:22:07,576
Your grandpa was so shy

257
00:22:07,659 --> 00:22:10,829
when he said this to me.

258
00:22:14,708 --> 00:22:16,084
<i>"One day,</i>

259
00:22:17,169 --> 00:22:18,837
<i>I found myself</i>

260
00:22:19,504 --> 00:22:22,382
<i>wanting you to be the first person
I saw in the morning."</i>

261
00:23:48,802 --> 00:23:53,807
{\an8}Subtitle translation by: Zensho Yamamoto

